Subject: [PATCH] cfg80211: notify background CAC abort after radar

The off-channel radar event cancels background_cac_done_wk before queuing
background_cac_abort_wk. Do not use the result of a second cancellation to
decide whether to notify userspace: the first cancellation is the normal
radar path, not evidence that CAC already completed. The background radar
owner check still prevents an abort notification after CAC completion.

---
diff --git a/net/wireless/mlme.c b/net/wireless/mlme.c
--- a/net/wireless/mlme.c
+++ b/net/wireless/mlme.c
@@ -1253,7 +1253,6 @@ __cfg80211_background_cac_event(struct cfg80211_registered_device *rdev,
 		break;
 	case NL80211_RADAR_CAC_ABORTED:
 		cfg80211_set_cac_state(wiphy, chandef, false);
-		if (!cancel_delayed_work(&rdev->background_cac_done_wk))
-			return;
+		cancel_delayed_work(&rdev->background_cac_done_wk);
 		break;
 	case NL80211_RADAR_CAC_STARTED:
